# [OUTPUT-DIR] Everything Deslop writes for a workspace — reports, logs,
# fingerprint/embedding caches, the live state file, IPC endpoint artifacts.
# One directory, one rule. `.deslop.toml` is config, not output, and stays
# tracked (this pattern is directory-only, so it does not match the file).
.deslop/

# Corpus clone cache. `make test-corpus` clones pinned public repositories
# here to measure accuracy and resource usage against real code. Clones are
# large (Flutter alone is ~200 MB) and fully reproducible from the pinned
# SHAs in `corpus/*.json`, so they are never tracked.
.corpus/

# Pre-[OUTPUT-DIR] cache location. Kept ignored only so that a checkout still
# holding one — written by an extension build from before the move, which may
# have a live `deslop.sock` bound inside it — does not show up as ~100 MB of
# untracked noise. Nothing writes here any more; the directory is safe to
# delete once no old `deslop-lsp` is running against it.
.deslop-cache/

# typeDiagram-generated IPC model code (source of truth: docs/models/*.td).
# Per CLAUDE.md the generated wire types must NOT be committed; they are
# regenerated on every cargo build by `crates/deslop-core/build.rs` and
# on every `make vsix-build` via the `typediagram-gen` Makefile target.
crates/deslop-core/src/wire_generated.rs
clients/vscode/src/types/wire-generated.ts


*.vsix


